# Line endings. The source this fork edits is LF; everything consumed by
# Windows or VMS tooling, and every binary, keeps what it shipped with.
#
# Converted 2026-09-01 (work log item 159) from a 55/53 split between
# upstream's CRLF and this fork's own LF. Nothing in the C++ needed CRLF:
# converting left all 64 object files byte-identical -- 31 from g++ 11 on
# Linux, 33 from mingw g++ 10 for Windows -- and windres produces the same
# .res from either input.
#
# "-text" everywhere means git stores and checks out byte for byte and
# never translates, so a clone on Windows with the default
# core.autocrlf=true cannot rewrite the tree. That makes the bytes in the
# repository the whole truth, which is why the exceptions below are listed
# rather than left to a heuristic.
* -text

# Binary. These were damaged once by a conversion sweep whose exclusion
# list was three extensions long, so the list is explicit now.
*.se1    binary
*.ttf    binary
*.pdf    binary
*.docx   binary
*.rtf    binary
*.png    binary
*.ico    binary
*.bmp    binary

# Windows and VMS tooling, left CRLF: Visual Studio's project files and
# resource editor, the module definition the Windows linker reads, the
# Internet Shortcut format Explorer parses, and a VMS DCL procedure.
# astrolog.rc is CRLF for the resource editor's sake; the generators that
# read it (tools/rc2qt.py and friends) take either.
*.sln     -text
*.vcproj  -text
*.vcxproj -text
*.rc      -text
*.def     -text
*.url     -text
*.com     -text

# Third-party font distributions, left exactly as they ship -- the table
# and the OFL FAQ that travel with them included.
font/** -text

# Data files the program itself parses, left exactly as they ship.
# Converting them is NOT cosmetic: with astrolog.as, atlas.as, timezone.as
# and nrvate.as converted to LF, tools/switch-matrix.sh moved six lines --
# "-0q" reported a different chart-info parse failure. Something in the
# data parsers reads a CR as content. Until that is found and fixed these
# stay as they are, and the diff is the evidence (work log item 159).
*.as   -text
*.csv  -text

# Swiss Ephemeris data the program reads the same way (the star list and
# the orbital elements), and upstream's shipped HTML documentation. Left
# as they ship for the same reason and to keep the diff against an
# upstream tarball readable.
sefstars.txt -text
seorbel.txt  -text
*.htm        -text
